  "message": "Good news first: the emulation shows no failures. The design itself held together, and all 8 components and their links were accepted. It's still marked \"blocked\" because none of our Google Cloud pieces (Pub/Sub, Dataflow, Vertex AI, BigQuery, Cloud Monitoring) has a native generator or emulator implementation yet, and the two existing systems still need a reference plan. That's product engineering work for the GCP streaming path. We can't fix it by redrawing the diagram, and we shouldn't shrink the design to storage, so I've left the board unchanged. The reproducer for that work is revision 2, artifact 93206bc4…, with 8 \"implementation needed\" or \"reference plan needed\" gaps. To shape the first contract that engineering builds, will the synthetic events include labelled anomalies, so we can test the real model on a time-based holdout instead of only the mock?",
